<p>I think we're more in agreement than it seems at first glance.</p>
<p>There are two parts to my suggestion for improved technobabble. The executive summary is vital of course. But just as important is limiting the length of the initial spiel.</p>
<p>TNG kept it to a half dozen sentences of babble. That seems a bit too restrictive in this case, but shorter than the current version definitely seems called for.</p>
<p>Tangent: I have a half-formed theory that crosslinks lead to less voting. Not because (or not <em>only</em> because) people don't like them. But because it leads readers off to other pages and some percentage of them won't come back to vote.</p>

